explanation_2024:
The open data principles are embedded in the National Updated eGovernment Strategy 2019-2025 - https://e-gov.bg/wps/wcm/connect/e-gov.bg-18083/1506d64e-0f16-4954-ba0b-dfd77ae58184/%D0%A1%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%B8%D1%8F+%D0%B7%D0%B0+%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%B5+%D0%BD%D0%B0+%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BE+%D1%83%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B5+2019-2025.pdf?MOD=AJPERES&CVID=nyx-ndJ&useDefaultText=0&useDefaultDesc=0
The Strategy provides for:
- the implementation of a Registry reform, which clearly provides for open data;
- decreasing the use of unstructured data;  
obligatory compliance with the open data principle (data generated by the public sector shall be in an open 
-machine-readable format, allowing for their reuse)

